<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēscensĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		descendo (postAug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a going down, descending</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balinearum,</span>”
				<i>into the bath</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 17, 69, § 178</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tiberina,</span>”
				<i>the sail down the Tiber</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 24, 70</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grando in descensione saltus,</span>”
				<i>upon the thickets</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 32, 19</span></i>
			.—Hence, * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>the bath
			itself</i>, Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβάσεις</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				5, 6, 26</span></i>.</div>
